  "type": "self",
  "prompt": "Let $f(x)=(x^2+8x+20)e^x$. Find $f^{(100)}(x)$.",
  "image": null,
  "choices": null,
  "answer": "$(x^2+208x+10720)e^x$",
  "acceptedAnswers": null,
  "answerUnit": null,
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Leibniz rule",
    "body": "By the Leibniz rule, with $h(x)=x^2+8x+20$ and $e^x$ (all of whose derivatives equal $e^x$): $f^{(100)}=\\sum_{k=0}^{100}\\binom{100}kh^{(k)}(x)e^x$. Only $k=0,1,2$ survive: $h=x^2+8x+20$, $h'=2x+8$, $h''=2$. So $f^{(100)}(x)=e^x\\left[x^2+8x+20+100(2x+8)+\\binom{100}2\\cdot2\\right]=e^x\\left[x^2+208x+(20+800+9900)\\right]=(x^2+208x+10720)e^x$.\n\n**Answer: $(x^2+208x+10720)e^x$**"
   }
  ],
