  "type": "numeric",
  "prompt": "Calculate the infinite series $$\\sum_{k=1}^\\infty\\frac1{2k^2-k}.$$",
  "image": null,
  "choices": null,
  "answer": "2*ln(2)",
  "answerDisplay": "$2\\ln 2$",
  "acceptedAnswers": null,
  "answerUnit": null,
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Partial fractions",
    "body": "$\\frac1{2k^2-k}=\\frac1{k(2k-1)}=\\frac2{2k-1}-\\frac2{2k}$. So the series is $2\\sum_{k\\ge1}\\left(\\frac1{2k-1}-\\frac1{2k}\\right)=2\\left(1-\\frac12+\\frac13-\\frac14+\\cdots\\right)=2\\ln2$ (the alternating harmonic series).\n\n**Answer: $2\\ln2$**"
   }
  ],
